# Slack Notification Configuration Template
# =============================================================================
# ⚠️  DO NOT commit actual credentials to Git!
# =============================================================================
#
# Usage:
#   1. Copy this file to slack.conf:
#      cp Scripts/config/slack.conf.example Scripts/config/slack.conf
#
#   2. Edit slack.conf and fill in your actual values
#
#   3. OR use environment variables (recommended for CI/CD):
#      export SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL="your-webhook-url"
#      export SLACK_BOT_TOKEN="your-bot-token"
#      export MSP_SLACK_DM_OVERRIDE="your-user-id"
#      export MSP_SLACK_ALERT_ENV="test"
#      export MSP_SLACK_TEST_WEBHOOK="your-test-webhook-url"
#
# Note: Environment variables take precedence over this config file.
# =============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# Configuration Architecture (Config-Driven Development)
# ============================================================================
#
# This project uses a layered configuration architecture:
#
# 1. Secrets Layer (THIS FILE - slack.conf, gitignored):
#    - SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, SLACK_BOT_TOKEN, MSP_SLACK_TEST_WEBHOOK
#    - Contains sensitive credentials only
#
# 2. Config Layer (slack_mapping.yaml, committed to git):
#    - email_map: Maps git user.email → Slack UserID (for smart DM routing)
#    - module_owner: Fallback routing when email not in map
#    - templates: Message templates with variable substitution
#    - Contains business logic and mappings, NO secrets
#
# 3. Logic Layer (notify.sh):
#    - Implements smart routing and notification delivery
#    - Reads secrets from THIS file, config from slack_mapping.yaml
#
# See: Scripts/config/slack_mapping.yaml for email_map and routing config
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# Basic Slack Configuration
# ============================================================================

# Slack Webhook URL (for channel notifications)
# Get from: Slack App → Incoming Webhooks → Add New Webhook
# Example: https://hooks.slack.com/services/T00000000/B00000000/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional Slack Configuration (uses defaults if not set)
# SLACK_CHANNEL=#releases
# SLACK_USERNAME=MSP iOS SDK Bot
# SLACK_ICON_EMOJI=:rocket:

# ============================================================================
# Advanced Slack Configuration
# ============================================================================

# Slack Bot Token (for DM and advanced API features)
# Get from: https://api.slack.com/apps → Your App → OAuth & Permissions
# Required for: Sending Direct Messages via MSP_SLACK_DM_OVERRIDE
# Example: xoxb-0000000000-0000000000000-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=

# ============================================================================
# Smart DM Routing vs Direct Message Override
# ============================================================================
#
# By DEFAULT, the system uses SMART ROUTING to automatically DM the release author:
#   1. Get git user.email from the release author
#   2. Look up UserID in email_map (slack_mapping.yaml)
#   3. Send DM to that UserID
#   4. Fallback: module_owner[module] → module_owner[default]
#
# Example Smart Routing:
#   - Release author: pengyu.gou@newsbreak.com
#   - email_map lookup: U0910UJPD7B
#   - Result: DM sent to U0910UJPD7B (automatic!)
#
# This ensures the ACTUAL release author gets notified, not a hardcoded person.
#
# ---
#
# Direct Message Override (Testing/Development Only)
# ONLY use this to OVERRIDE smart routing for testing purposes.
# When set, ALL DMs go to this UserID regardless of who the release author is.
#
# WARNING: When enabled, smart routing is BYPASSED!
#
# Find User ID: Right-click user in Slack → View Profile → More → Copy member ID
# Example: U0910UJPD7B
#
# Leave EMPTY to enable smart routing (recommended for production):
MSP_SLACK_DM_OVERRIDE=

# Slack Alert Environment Mode
# Values: test, prod (default: prod)
# - test: Uses MSP_SLACK_TEST_WEBHOOK, safe for testing
# - prod: Uses SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, sends to production channel
MSP_SLACK_ALERT_ENV=prod

# Test Webhook URL (used when MSP_SLACK_ALERT_ENV=test)
# Separate webhook for testing to avoid spamming production channels
# Create in: Slack App → Incoming Webhooks → Add New Webhook (test channel)
# Example: https://hooks.slack.com/services/T00000000/B00000000/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
MSP_SLACK_TEST_WEBHOOK=

# ============================================================================
# Usage Examples
# ============================================================================
#
# 1. Production Release with Smart Routing (Recommended):
#    # DM is automatically sent to the release author via email_map
#    export MSP_SLACK_ALERT_ENV=prod
#    unset MSP_SLACK_DM_OVERRIDE  # Enable smart routing
#    ./Scripts/msp-release.sh run <version>
#
#    How it works:
#    - System gets your git user.email
#    - Looks up your UserID in email_map (slack_mapping.yaml)
#    - Sends DM to YOUR Slack account
#    - No manual configuration needed!
#
# 2. Test Release with Smart Routing:
#    export MSP_SLACK_ALERT_ENV=test  # Use test webhook
#    unset MSP_SLACK_DM_OVERRIDE      # Enable smart routing
#    ./Scripts/msp-release.sh run <version>
#
# 3. Override Smart Routing (Testing Only):
#    # Force all DMs to a specific user (bypasses smart routing)
#    export MSP_SLACK_DM_OVERRIDE=U0910UJPD7B
#    ./Scripts/msp-release.sh run <version>
#
#    ⚠️  WARNING: This disables smart routing!
#    Use only for debugging or when you need all DMs to go to one person.
#
# 4. Add yourself to Smart Routing:
#    # If you're a new team member and want to receive DMs automatically:
#    1. Get your Slack UserID:
#       Right-click your name in Slack → View Profile → More → Copy member ID
#    2. Edit Scripts/config/slack_mapping.yaml
#    3. Add to email_map section:
#       your.email@newsbreak.com: U0XXXXXXXXX
#    4. Commit and push the change
#    5. Now all your releases will DM you automatically!
#
# ============================================================================
# Quick Setup for New Users
# ============================================================================
#
# Step 1: Copy this template
#   cp Scripts/config/slack.conf.example Scripts/config/slack.conf
#
# Step 2: Fill in secrets (get from team lead or Slack App settings)
#   SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/T04Q2K244/...
#   SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
#   MSP_SLACK_TEST_WEBHOOK=https://hooks.slack.com/services/T04Q2K244/...
#
# Step 3: Add yourself to email_map (optional but recommended)
#   Edit Scripts/config/slack_mapping.yaml:
#   email_map:
#     your.email@newsbreak.com: U0XXXXXXXXX  # Your Slack UserID
#
# Step 4: Test
#   export MSP_SLACK_ALERT_ENV=test
#   source Scripts/notify/slack.sh
#   load_slack_config
#   test_slack_notification
#
# Done! Smart routing will now automatically DM you on releases.
#
